OL,3,ANato chief vows defence against space
OL,4,Athreat after Russian nuclear satellite
OL,5,Areports
OL,6,
OL,7,FNato chief Mark Rutte has said the
OL,8,Falliance will defend against any
OL,9,Fthreats in space after reports that
OL,10,FRussia was preparing to launch a
OL,11,Fnuclear-armed satellite.
OL,13,FIntelligence reports about a possible
OL,14,Flaunch in the next 60 days had been
OL,15,Fshared among Nato countries this month,
OL,16,Faccording to German media outlets. It
OL,17,Fwas not clear which country had
OL,18,Fauthored the reports.
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG11/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,0,100
PN,11912
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F119A1795515953
OL,1,W5j 5Q7kjs15j 5ws
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ANato chief vows defence against space
OL,4,Athreat after Russian nuclear satellite
OL,5,Areports
OL,6,
OL,7,FAsked about the reports, Rutte said:
OL,8,F"We will always make sure we defend
OL,9,Fevery inch of Nato territory, and that
OL,10,Fincludes making sure we are safe when
OL,11,Fit comes to the space element."
OL,13,FKremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said he
OL,14,Fhadn't seen the latest reports but
OL,15,Fdismissed reports citing "unknown
OL,16,Fsources" as "hardly worth taking
OL,17,Fseriously".
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG12/39
